  "edits": [
    {
      "what": "before the USB host looks for an interface's driver, an older keyboard's is made to say it is MIDI",
      "hook": "_hook_adopt",
      "device_address": "0x8000a3e0",
      "file_offset": "0x35d8c",
      "expected": "00 e8 0c 00",
      "new": "64 e2 10 2e",
      "evidence": "[code] 'LINK 0x30', the start of the routine that walks the drivers (list 0x080198ac) for a device (R0) and interface (R1); its one caller is 0x8000aef8"
    },
    {
      "what": "after the audio/MIDI driver read a MIDI interface, its endpoints get a port count if they had none",
      "hook": "_hook_endpoints",
      "device_address": "0x80003bbe",
